#
#   <release tag>  <asset file name>  <sha256>
#
# The asset is attached to the GitHub Release with that tag. fetch-assets.sh
# downloads each one and refuses to continue if its checksum differs from the
# one committed here, so changing a tarball means a new release AND a commit
# to this file -- never a silent re-upload.
#
# Every *.tar.gz fetched is unpacked at / in the image (see Dockerfile), so the
# directory each tarball unpacks to is the path consumers COPY from.

